27:["$","section","2-Use an evidence map for research fit",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-3","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Use an evidence map for research fit"}],[["$","p","Create a short research-fit map before writing your statement. In a fictional engineering case, an applicant has used a simulation method in a final-year project and wants to investigate its limits on a different dataset. The useful evidence is the question, the method they actually used, one result and the limitation they can explain. “I am passionate about innovation” does not supply that evidence.",{"children":"Create a short research-fit map before writing your statement. In a fictional engineering case, an applicant has used a simulation method in a final-year project and wants to investigate its limits on a different dataset. The useful evidence is the question, the method they actually used, one result and the limitation they can explain. “I am passionate about innovation” does not supply that evidence."}],["$","p","Add why the proposed school or group is suitable, using its actual research rather than copying a profile. Mark methods you have not learned as development needs. Follow the programme’s instructions about supervisor contact, proposal, personal statement, references and any video or test requirement. A positive faculty conversation can help you refine a plan, but it is not an admission offer or scholarship decision.",{"children":"Add why the proposed school or group is suitable, using its actual research rather than copying a profile. Mark methods you have not learned as development needs. Follow the programme’s instructions about supervisor contact, proposal, personal statement, references and any video or test requirement. A positive faculty conversation can help you refine a plan, but it is not an admission offer or scholarship decision."}]],"$undefined",[["$","p",null,{"className":"table-scroll-hint","children":"On a small screen, scroll the table sideways to compare all columns."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-table-wrap","role":"region","aria-label":"Original research-fit worksheet","tabIndex":0,"children":["$","table",null,{"className":"guide-table","children":[["$","caption",null,{"children":"Original research-fit worksheet"}],["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[[["$","th","Your evidence",{"scope":"col","children":"Your evidence"}],["$","th","Specific entry to prepare",{"scope":"col","children":"Specific entry to prepare"}],["$","th","Honest boundary",{"scope":"col","children":"Honest boundary"}]],"$undefined"]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Prior work"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"Question,method and one result"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"Do not claim the whole team’s work"}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","tr","1",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Proposed study"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"A manageable next question"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"Not a finished thesis promise"}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","tr","2",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"School fit"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"Relevant expertise or facilities"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"No invented supervisor agreement"}]],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}]}],"$undefined"],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
28:["$","section","3-Read the stipend and support period as written",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-4","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Read the stipend and support period as written"}],[["$","p","The central RSS table effectiveJanuary 2026 lists international-student monthly stipends of S$3,000 for PhD and S$2,900 for research master’s candidates, alongside annual tuition coverage. These are the current published rates, not a newly announced 2027 increase. The award is initially tenable for one year and renewal depends on progress; the stated maximum support is two years for a master’s and four for a PhD, subject to the school and research funding.",{"children":"The central RSS table effectiveJanuary 2026 lists international-student monthly stipends of S$3,000 for PhD and S$2,900 for research master’s candidates, alongside annual tuition coverage. These are the current published rates, not a newly announced 2027 increase. The award is initially tenable for one year and renewal depends on progress; the stated maximum support is two years for a master’s and four for a PhD, subject to the school and research funding."}],["$","p","The admission guide’s maximum candidature and the scholarship’s maximum support need not be the same. Put both in your record and ask how any additional period would be financed. Do not budget the maximum stipend, a possible post-qualifying increase or an extension as already awarded. Your offer and applicable award conditions determine actual coverage and continuation.",{"children":"The admission guide’s maximum candidature and the scholarship’s maximum support need not be the same. Put both in your record and ask how any additional period would be financed. Do not budget the maximum stipend, a possible post-qualifying increase or an extension as already awarded. Your offer and applicable award conditions determine actual coverage and continuation."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined",["$","p",null,{"className":"table-source","children":["Official reference: ",[["$","span","https://www.ntu.edu.sg/admissions/graduate/financialmatters/scholarships/rss",{"children":["",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://www.ntu.edu.sg/admissions/graduate/financialmatters/scholarships/rss","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":"NTU: Research Scholarship terms and current stipend table"}]]}]]]}],"$undefined"]}]
29:["$","section","4-No bond does not mean no scholarship duties",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-5","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"No bond does not mean no scholarship duties"}],[["$","p","NTU states that RSS has no bond, while international scholars must fulfil Graduate Assistantship Programme teaching or laboratory-supervision duties. Those statements concern different obligations and can both be true. Before accepting, read the applicable duties, academic expectations and approval rules rather than interpreting “no bond” as freedom from all scholarship conditions.",{"children":"NTU states that RSS has no bond, while international scholars must fulfil Graduate Assistantship Programme teaching or laboratory-supervision duties. Those statements concern different obligations and can both be true. Before accepting, read the applicable duties, academic expectations and approval rules rather than interpreting “no bond” as freedom from all scholarship conditions."}],["$","p","Make an original weekly planning record with research, required coursework and scholarship duties on separate lines. Use it to identify questions about workload and supervision; do not invent an official hours allocation. If an obligation is unclear, ask the school how it is scheduled and documented. Keep written clarification with the award terms so a later assumption does not become a dispute.",{"children":"Make an original weekly planning record with research, required coursework and scholarship duties on separate lines. Use it to identify questions about workload and supervision; do not invent an official hours allocation. If an obligation is unclear, ask the school how it is scheduled and documented. Keep written clarification with the award terms so a later assumption does not become a dispute."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined",["$","p",null,{"className":"table-source","children":["Official reference: ",[["$","span","https://www.ntu.edu.sg/admissions/graduate/financialmatters/scholarships/rss",{"children":["",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://www.ntu.edu.sg/admissions/graduate/financialmatters/scholarships/rss","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":"NTU: Research Scholarship terms and current stipend table"}]]}]]]}],"$undefined"]}]
2a:["$","section","5-Prepare cash before the first payment",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-6","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Prepare cash before the first payment"}],[["$","p","A monthly stipend does not settle the timing of every arrival expense. NTU asks new students to update Singapore bank details before the 15th of the commencement month to avoid stipend delays. That administrative instruction is not a promise that a student without completed arrangements will receive money on a chosen day.",{"children":"A monthly stipend does not settle the timing of every arrival expense. NTU asks new students to update Singapore bank details before the 15th of the commencement month to avoid stipend delays. That administrative instruction is not a promise that a student without completed arrangements will receive money on a chosen day."}],["$","p","Use a fictional arrival worksheet: assume S$1,200 refundable housing deposit,S$800 travel and S$1,000 initial living costs. The initial cash requirement is S$3,000 before any confirmed reimbursement or payment. Keep the deposit’s return conditions separate from spending and replace all assumptions with real quotes. List the account, registration and award tasks on which payment depends, then decide how to cover the interval if any task takes longer.",{"children":"Use a fictional arrival worksheet: assume S$1,200 refundable housing deposit,S$800 travel and S$1,000 initial living costs. The initial cash requirement is S$3,000 before any confirmed reimbursement or payment. Keep the deposit’s return conditions separate from spending and replace all assumptions with real quotes. List the account, registration and award tasks on which payment depends, then decide how to cover the interval if any task takes longer."}]],"$undefined",[["$","p",null,{"className":"table-scroll-hint","children":"On a small screen, scroll the table sideways to compare all columns."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-table-wrap","role":"region","aria-label":"Original arrival-cash exercise: all costs assumed","tabIndex":0,"children":["$","table",null,{"className":"guide-table","children":[["$","caption",null,{"children":"Original arrival-cash exercise: all costs assumed"}],["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[[["$","th","Line",{"scope":"col","children":"Line"}],["$","th","Amount",{"scope":"col","children":"Amount"}],["$","th","Treatment",{"scope":"col","children":"Treatment"}]],"$undefined"]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Refundable deposit"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"S$1,200"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"Cash tied up; refund conditions apply"}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","tr","1",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Travel"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"S$800"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"Check any actual coverage separately"}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","tr","2",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Initial living"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"S$1,000"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"Money needed before reliable payment"}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","tr","3",{"children":[[["$","th","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Initial cash total"}],["$","td","1",{"children":"S$3,000"}],["$","td","2",{"children":"Not an official NTU cost estimate"}]],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}]}],"$undefined"],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined",["$","p",null,{"className":"table-source","children":["Official reference: ",[["$","span","https://www.ntu.edu.sg/admissions/graduate/financialmatters/scholarships/rss",{"children":["",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://www.ntu.edu.sg/admissions/graduate/financialmatters/scholarships/rss","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":"NTU: Research Scholarship terms and current stipend table"}]]}]]]}],"$undefined"]}]
2b:["$","section","6-Check the admission form and scholarship interest together",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-7","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Check the admission form and scholarship interest together"}],[["$","p","NTU’s scholarship FAQ says a separate scholarship application is not required for the described process: applicants indicate interest in the admission application and the school assesses them. Follow the actual form and chosen programme; ticking interest is a request for consideration, not an award. Retain the complete submitted application and any later instructions.",{"children":"NTU’s scholarship FAQ says a separate scholarship application is not required for the described process: applicants indicate interest in the admission application and the school assesses them. Follow the actual form and chosen programme; ticking interest is a request for consideration, not an award. Retain the complete submitted application and any later instructions."}],["$","p","Before submitting, inspect the exact degree/intake, evidence fields, reference arrangements and scholarship selection. Keep admission and funding outcomes as separate statuses until the offer explains both. If you receive an offer, read duration, tuition, stipend, duties and continuation conditions together, then compare them with your budget. Use the owner’s current instructions for any acceptance or banking step; this guide has not tested an authenticated application account.",{"children":"Before submitting, inspect the exact degree/intake, evidence fields, reference arrangements and scholarship selection. Keep admission and funding outcomes as separate statuses until the offer explains both. If you receive an offer, read duration, tuition, stipend, duties and continuation conditions together, then compare them with your budget. Use the owner’s current instructions for any acceptance or banking step; this guide has not tested an authenticated application account."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined",["$","p",null,{"className":"table-source","children":["Official reference: ",[["$","span","https://www.ntu.edu.sg/admissions/graduate/financialmatters/scholarships/frequently-asked-questions",{"children":["",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://www.ntu.edu.sg/admissions/graduate/financialmatters/scholarships/frequently-asked-questions","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":"NTU: scholarship application process FAQ"}]]}]]]}],"$undefined"]}]
